  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 301 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nOnce the front passes through, Tuesday will feel much cooler as\nmore seasonable temperatures return. One note for behind the \nfront is the potential for smoke in the air, possibly even \nreduced air quality at the surface. GOES Geocolor satellite\nSunday afternoon indicated widespread smoke over the northern \nCONUS Rockies into the western Dakotas. RAP and HRRR extended \nsmoke forecasts indicate this being steered southward behind the\nfront over our area. This is still too far out to tell if it \nwould mix to near- surface, but at least some smoky sky tonight\ninto early Tuesday looks probable.\n\nAfter quiet and near to slightly warmer than seasonable\ntemperatures Wednesday and into the day Thursday, a slow moving\nand fairly well-defined short wave is indicated by guidance to \npass over the area late Thursday night into Friday. This looks \nlike the next chance of rain.",
